            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "World's top sugar maker shuts large Brazil plant to cut debt",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Raizen SA, the world's largest sugar producer, said on Tuesday that it was shutting down for an indefinite period one of its largest plants in Brazil, the Santa Elisa mill, as the company continues to adopt measures to deal with a large debt load.  Raizen, which is controlled by Shell and Brazilian conglomerate Cosan SA, said that as a result of the plant's closure it had entered into agreements with six sugar companies to sell 3.5 million metric tons of sugarcane that would be processed by the Santa Elisa mill.  It said the sale of that sugarcane would bring in 1.045 billion reais ($188.18 million) that Raizen will use to cut its debt of over 30 billion reais.",
